                  2 post-randomization events likely to impact accurate
                  assessment of pain outcomes beyond 5 years in trial
                  participants: loss to follow-up and total knee replacement
                  (TKR). We conducted literature searches for covariates related
                  to pain and TKR in individuals with knee OA and combined these
                  with expert input. We synthesized the evidence into graphical
                  models. RESULTS: We identified 94 potential covariates
                  potentially related to pain and/or TKR among individuals with
                  knee OA. Of these, 46 were identified in the literature review
                  and 48 by expert panelists. We determined that adjustment for
                  50 covariates may be required to estimate the long-term
                  effects of knee OA treatments on pain. CONCLUSION: We present
                  a process for combining literature reviews with expert input
